body:
Fixes #12482
Clause-②: no. The panel draws more of the bound row it already reads; no type, prop, export, page node or spec declaration changes.

## What changes

The decision panel (`record:approval_decision`), which objectstack's served `sys_approval_request_detail` page already mounts in its `actions` slot, now draws a **"Waiting on"** row between the tally and the decisions. Each pending approver is one chip:

- the server's own name for a user id (`pending_approver_names`, from the same approvals get the page reads);
- for a `position:NAME` slot the server left unnamed, the position's registry label, with the people who hold it;
- the countersign group the slot fills (`pending_approver_groups`, on a `per_group` node), as `· Finance`;
- one person holding several quorum slots is one chip with a count (`Ada Lovelace ×3`, objectui#12077's case); two people sharing a name in two groups stay two chips;
- an id nothing can name keeps the identity formatter's middle-truncated face (`zzUnre…z123`), the face the inbox's sheet draws for it. Every raw slot stays in the chip's `title`, on hover only.

The drawing reuses app-shell's one approver-naming path, the one the business record's approvals panel already draws its chips with: `approverChips` over `approverDisplay`, and `useApproverDirectory` for references the server left unnamed. Files: `packages/app-shell/src/views/approval-decision/ApprovalDecisionPanel.tsx` (+ its test), one console test, one changeset. `ApprovalsInboxPage` (the sheet) is not touched (ADR-0060 rule 3), and nothing is exported.

## Fit before build (the ruling's item 2), measured

- **The block that carries the face is the one the page already has.** `record:approval_decision` is a declared spec type with an empty strict props row, and the panel reads the bound request row. At objectstack `57994c311f` the approvals get serves `pending_approvers`, `pending_approver_names` (the service's display enrichment) and, on a `per_group` node, `pending_approver_groups` (set beside `decision_progress`). The spec's approval-service contract declares both name maps as display enrichment. So the face needs **no spec row, no page edit and no new block**.
- **`DecisionProgressIndicator` cannot carry it without a contract change.** It draws a tally, and its own docblock says a caller renders it only when the tally is present. A `first_response` node carries no `decision_progress`, so the indicator is not drawn there at all, while that node's approver is still waiting. The sheet and the business record's approvals panel both draw the tally and the names as two parts under two gates (tally present; pending request with at least one slot). The panel does the same. `approval-progress/**` is unchanged.

## The PM's mechanism assumptions, measured

- **A1 holds.** The panel already holds the row: it read `pending_approvers` for the eligible count before this change.
- **A2 holds, with the cost named.** A slate the get named whole costs **0** extra requests (pinned). A `position:` slot the server left unnamed costs:
  - the metadata store's `ensureType('position')`, one `GET /api/v1/meta/position` per session, shared with every other reader of the store;
  - the staffing leg: one `sys_user_position` find, plus one `sys_user` find when the seat has holders;
  - `team:` and `department:` slots: one find per directory object.

  All reads are `$in`-batched, once per slate per page session, through a module cache the decision buttons on the same request share. So at most 3 reads per page, whatever the number of approvers. Per approver: none. The sheet's own path reads only `ensureType('position')`. The app-shell path also names the seat's holders, as the business record's panel already does.
- **A3: the sheet's face is matched; its "and N more" form does not exist.** The sheet draws its "Waiting on" row on a pending request with a slot:
  - one chip per (name, group);
  - the server name first, then the identity formatter (a position's registry label or prettified name, `Role: X`, an email as is, a long id middle-truncated);
  - the group as `· G`, duplicates as `×N`, first-seen order, raw ids in `title`.

  The sheet has no "and N more" form. Its only "more" strings are the list's load-more. So nothing of that shape is matched.
- **A4 is false on the served page: no raw approver id is printed there today.** The served page's Details tab is a bare `record:details`. Since objectui#12433 that draws the object's `highlightFields` minus the strip's fields, which leaves `record_id` alone. `pending_approvers` is not a highlight field. Measured on the real `RecordDetailView` over `ApprovalRecordReads`, before this change, with a three-slot slate: the approver ids appear **0** times on the served page. The "More details" print objectui#12077 measured is the **synthesized** page, used when no page is served: the same probe there prints the ids 3 times, and the decision panel is not mounted on that page.

  The spec declares `pending_approvers` as `Field.textarea`, a comma-separated slot store that mixes user ids, `position:` and `role:` refs and emails, not a user reference. So "draw the field by name" does not apply, and on the served page there is nothing to hide.

## Pins

- `ApprovalDecisionPanel.test.tsx`, a new describe block covering:
  - two same-name people in two groups;
  - one person in three quorum slots;
  - a position's registry label and holder;
  - CONTROL: the server's name wins and nothing is asked;
  - CONTROL: an unnamed id is middle-truncated;
  - CONTROL: no pending approvers;
  - CONTROL: a decided request names no one;
  - a `first_response` node with no tally still names its approver.
- `apps/console/src/services/approvalRequestsDataSource.servedPageApprovers-12482.test.tsx`: the served page, copied whole, on the real `RecordDetailView` under the console's `ApprovalRecordReads`, with only the transport, the console adapter and the metadata store doubled. It pins:
  - named approvers with groups and a position label;
  - no pending approver id printed anywhere on the page;
  - objectui#12077's three-slot case;
  - no directory read for a server-named slate;
  - CONTROL: no pending approvers;
  - CONTROL: an unresolvable id drawn as the sheet draws it.

  It lives in `apps/console` because the routed source it mounts is console code.

## Ablation (one-shot, not kept)

The fix was committed first (`233965379b`). The script mutated `ApprovalDecisionPanel.tsx`, dropping the `PendingApprovers` element for a marker comment:

- the anchor count went 1 to 0 and the marker count 0 to 1;
- **10 pins went red**: the 6 naming pins in the panel suite and the 4 in the served-page suite;
- 17 stayed green: the controls (no slots, a decided request, no directory read) and the suites' pre-existing tests.

Restore: `git checkout HEAD --` the path, then a blob-hash match against `HEAD`, with `git diff HEAD` empty, under a `trap` on EXIT, INT and TERM. No build sits between: the root vitest config aliases every `@object-ui` specifier to source, so the pins read the edited file.

## Gates (local subset; the full farm is CI's)

All local readings are at `233965379b` (the branch head), with each exit code captured before any pipe.

- **Dependency closure build:** `pnpm turbo run build --filter='@object-ui/console^...' --concurrency=2`, run so the type-checks read built declarations. Exit 0; 34 tasks, 28 of them cache hits.
- **`pnpm --filter @object-ui/app-shell type-check`** (`tsc --noEmit && tsc -p tsconfig.test.json`): exit 0. The test project's include glob, `src/**/*.test.tsx`, covers the panel's suite. That is read off the glob, not counted with `--listFiles`.
- **`apps/console` `tsc --noEmit --listFiles`:** exit 0. The new pin is in the file list (1 hit).
- **vitest, one run, 47 files, 391 tests, all passed, exit 0:**
  - `approval-decision/` and `approval-progress/`;
  - every `approvalRequestsDataSource.*` suite and `AppContent.approvalRecordReads`;
  - all of `apps/console/src/pages/system/`, which holds the `ApprovalsInboxPage.*` pins, run as the CONTROL;
  - `RecordApprovalsPanel*`, the two `RecordDetailView` approval suites, `global-page-blocks.render`, `DeclaredActionsBar.overrideAffordance`, `useApproverDirectory.contractEnvelope-5945` and `approverIdentity*`.
- **Census and ratchet tests whose subject the diff touches, one run, 18 files, 696 tests, all passed, exit 0:**
  - in app-shell: `product-neutral-renderer.ratchet`, `no-component-any-cast`, `no-refresh-key-remount`, `adr0054-ratchet`, `defaults-maps-mirror-en-pack`, `writeRefusalCensus-11583`;
  - in i18n and components: `ariaLabelLiteralCensus-12145`, `machineLocaleCensus-9909`, `dead-pack-keys-retired-8754`, `iconOnlyButtonCensus-12143`;
  - script suites: `check-i18n-call-site-keys`, the three `check-vi-mock-*`, `one-authority-per-exported-name-6273`, `check-control-bytes`;
  - registration: `registry-inputs-spec-parity`, `record-approval-decision-arm-12342`.
- **Check scripts, each exit 0:**
  - `check:control-bytes` and `check:new-line-citations` (0 new citations);
  - `check:i18n-keys` and `check:i18n-drift`;
  - the three `check:vi-mock-*` and `check:test-path-roots`;
  - `check:changeset-claims` and `check:pending-changeset-literals`;
  - `check:handler-key-reads`, `check:metadata-write-doors` and `check:unreferenced-sources`;
  - `check-changeset-no-major`, `-overwrite`, `-presence` and `-fixed`.
- **eslint on the three changed source and test files:** exit 0, no findings.
- **Left to CI, not run here:**
  - `pnpm lint`, repo-wide;
  - the `pnpm test` shards;
  - Bundle Analysis (the eager closure needs a full console build);
  - `check:sdui-registration-pins`, which reads a full build;
  - `check:i18n-designer-parity` (no label was added and no pack changed).

## Acceptance notes

- **Out of this face, measured, not filed (for the seat): the submitter's raw id.** On the served page the highlights strip prints `submitter_id`, declared `Field.lookup('sys_user')`, as the bare id. The approvals get serves the id plus `submitter_name`, never an expansion. The strip made no label read: `findOne` was never called, no `sys_user` read was made, and the served `submitter_name` was not shown.
  - This holds before and after this change.
  - Measured in the harness on the real `RecordDetailView` under `ApprovalRecordReads`, not on a live server.
  - The landing site is the seat's call: the get route serving the lookup expanded, or the lookup display reading a served name. A consumer-side reshape in the routed source would be the tolerant fallback AGENTS.md #0.1 refuses.
  - The served-page pin here asserts approver ids only.
- **The synthesized page still prints the slot store** under "More details" (objectui#12077's original reading), on hosts that serve no `sys_approval_request_detail` page. This face does not reach it: the panel is not mounted there. The fix would be producer-side (the object's declaration) or a route-scoped hide, both off this surface.
- The tally's "N eligible approver(s)" counts slots, not people: one person in three quorum slots reads "3 eligible approver(s)" beside one `×3` chip. The sheet and the business record's panel count the same way, and the count's meaning (slots or people) is not declared anywhere. Noted, not changed.
- The chip markup is now drawn in two app-shell places from one `approverChips` output: this panel and the business record's approvals panel (outside this card's file surface). The closing card that retires the sheet is the natural place to fold them into one.

